    "updated_at": "2026-11-24T03:10:06Z",
    "body": "Port onto the current frame, head `f99a9d736`.\n\n- The branch merges the #2969 port (`d3443eddc`). That head includes main `44e6a8269`, with the zero-step writer of #2984 and the inspection setup of #3219. There was no rebase and no force-push.\n- The old `jescript.rs` writer is gone. The open cut now uses the zero-step writer: `agie_setup::CutoffSetup20` writes `c_left` or `c_right`, `stp1` and `stp2` in air, `ID_SEPCUT \"0.0\"` and ASDELETE only. ASAGIE is gone.\n- A closed cycle keeps the 1.0 mm separation rule. A closed cycle with 0.0 is still refused (`an_open_cut_posts_zero_steps_and_no_separation_and_a_closed_cut_keeps_one_millimetre`).\n- The CCSEP20 and DIE20 goldens do not change. The new golden is `LOWER20.SBL`.\n- Offline control import on 2026-11-24, for `LOWER20` and `UPPER20`: `CCB030[0]` after import, the left or right side, an open contour with entry `stp1` and exit `stp2`, and no separation. After TECCUT: `CCB030[4]`, offsets 245, 155, 140 and 134 µm, and `geen fouten`. The plots show four passes with one crossing each, at the same Y values as the earlier control run of this PR. The PR body has the details.\n- Quick gate: 1190 steps, 1 red step that is not in this diff (`rotary_verify`, red on main since #3774). Clippy is clean.\n",
